Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Clear foreground when macOS focus leaves Wine

The desktop window is not an active application. The regular foreground
setter clears the foreground input when passed the desktop; the internal
setter instead activates Explorer's desktop window. Use the clearing path
for both macOS window and app deactivation.

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -1904,7 +1904,7 @@
     {
         send_message(hwnd, WM_CANCELMODE, 0, 0);
         if (hwnd == NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
-            NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
+            NtUserSetForegroundWindow(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
     }
 }
 
@@ -1932,8 +1932,8 @@
 
     if (get_active_window() == NtUserGetForegroundWindow())
     {
-        TRACE("setting fg to desktop\n");
-        NtUserSetForegroundWindowInternal(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
+        TRACE("clearing foreground window\n");
+        NtUserSetForegroundWindow(NtUserGetDesktopWindow());
     }
 }
 
